      },
      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CallBackery versions before 0.62.0 for Perl accept session cookies of any age sent in the X-Session-Cookie header.\n\ncookieConf() rejects a cookie older than 300 seconds only when it arrives in the xsc query parameter. The same cookie sent in the X-Session-Cookie header is accepted however old it is.\n\nA session cookie that leaks through a log, a Referer header or browser history authenticates as its user indefinitely.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
